Here is the complete report of the "Memo" entity definition across all four layers in this repository.

---

## 1. SQL Schema

The `memo` table is defined in three dialect-specific `LATEST.sql` migration files, all with the same logical columns:

- **`/bench/repo/store/migration/sqlite/LATEST.sql`** -- line 33
- **`/bench/repo/store/migration/postgres/LATEST.sql`** -- line 32
- **`/bench/repo/store/migration/mysql/LATEST.sql`** -- line 32

Columns (SQLite version as representative):

| Column       | Type    | Notes                                           |
|--------------|---------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `id`         | INTEGER | PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT                        |
| `uid`        | TEXT    | NOT NULL UNIQUE                                  |
| `creator_id` | INTEGER | NOT NULL                                         |
| `created_ts` | BIGINT  | NOT NULL, defaults to epoch seconds of `now()`   |
| `updated_ts` | BIGINT  | NOT NULL, defaults to epoch seconds of `now()`   |
| `row_status` | TEXT    | CHECK IN ('NORMAL', 'ARCHIVED'), default 'NORMAL'|
| `content`    | TEXT    | NOT NULL, default ''                             |
| `visibility` | TEXT    | CHECK IN ('PUBLIC','PROTECTED','PRIVATE'), default 'PRIVATE' |
| `pinned`     | INTEGER | 0 or 1, default 0                               |
| `payload`    | TEXT    | NOT NULL, default '{}'                           |

Postgres uses `SERIAL`, `JSONB`, and `BOOLEAN`; MySQL uses `INT AUTO_INCREMENT`, `JSON`, `VARCHAR(256)`, and `BOOLEAN` -- same logical schema.

There are also companion tables `memo_relation` and `memo_share` in the same files.

---

## 2. Go Store Model

**`/bench/repo/store/memo.go`** -- line 35

```go
type Memo struct {
    ID         int32
    UID        string
    RowStatus  RowStatus
    CreatorID  int32
    CreatedTs  int64
    UpdatedTs  int64
    Content    string
    Visibility Visibility
    Pinned     bool
    Payload    *storepb.MemoPayload
    ParentUID  *string
}
```

The same file also defines companion types `FindMemo` (line 57), `FindMemoPayload` (line 84), and `UpdateMemo` (line 93). The `Visibility` type is defined at line 13 with constants `Public`, `Protected`, and `Private`. The `Payload` field references `storepb.MemoPayload`, which is the generated Go code from the store-layer protobuf (see below).

---

## 3. API Proto Message

**Primary API message:** **`/bench/repo/proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto`** -- line 198

```protobuf
message Memo {
  string name = 1;                           // resource name "memos/{memo}"
  State state = 2;
  string creator = 3;                        // "users/{user}"
  google.protobuf.Timestamp create_time = 4;
  google.protobuf.Timestamp update_time = 5;
  string content = 7;                        // Markdown
  Visibility visibility = 9;
  repeated string tags = 10;
  bool pinned = 11;
  repeated Attachment attachments = 12;
  repeated MemoRelation relations = 13;
  repeated Reaction reactions = 14;
  Property property = 15;
  optional string parent = 16;              // "memos/{memo}"
  string snippet = 17;
  optional Location location = 18;

  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    string title = 5;
  }
}
```

**Store-layer payload protobuf:** **`/bench/repo/proto/store/memo.proto`** -- line 7

This defines `MemoPayload` (not `Memo` itself), which is the serialized JSON payload stored in the `payload` column of the SQL table:

```protobuf
message MemoPayload {
  Property property = 1;
  Location location = 2;
  repeated string tags = 3;
  // ... nested Property and Location messages
}
```

